{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans","id":1446763,"title":"Do Gangrel diablerize each other more than other clans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-01T02:31:41-07:00","id":1446763,"title":"Do Gangrel diablerize each other more than other clans?","content":"I mean, they are out on the road much more than other clans, isolated, no witnesses if two Gangrel run across each other and one decides to eat the other. I'd think diablerie would be pretty common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:46:04-07:00","id":1446764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans#post1446763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they are out on the road much more than other clans, isolated, no witnesses if two Gangrel run across each other and one decides to eat the other. I'd think diablerie would be pretty common.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd argue probably not because:<br /> <br /> 1. The majority of diablerists were going to be members of one Warring Sect for another. During wartime, you can kill whoever you want and no one will care.<br /> <br /> 2. The thing about Gangrel on the Road are going to be that they're not going to run into one another nearly as often as Kindred that are congregated in one specific area like Elysium or not. I mean, Yellowstone is pretty huge even for Kindred stalking the campsites.<br /> <br /> 3. Gangrel are generally more in touch with their Beast than most Kindred. If only by 20% or so. If they're going to diablerize someone, it's going to be very deliberate versus Kindred who lose control and sink their fangs into a guy.<br /> <br /> 4. Gangrel are also good at taking the measure of other Kindred. The Big Dog will not eat the Little Dog and the Little Dog is not stupid.<br /> <br /> 5. Depending on the Prince, Blood Hunts are already guilt-free power offers. It may destroy your social cred to eat Annabelle once Kevin Jackson gets sick of her and piss off all her friends but it's legal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T03:44:22-07:00","id":1446770,"title":"","content":"I imagine no, but I also imagine that's a common rumor or stereotype about them (and also Ravnos) or any Kindred who chooses to spend significant amounts of time away from Kindred society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T10:29:50-07:00","id":1446809,"title":"","content":"Nos have a pretty decent advantage in both choice and shelter. They'd most likely Diablerize the most. <br /> <br /> In times of yore, many gangrel were rather anti-establisment and could conceivable sweep the much smaller settlements for vampires to devour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:09:10-07:00","id":1446822,"title":"","content":"I agree with the above posters. It's a stereotype that Ventrue and Toreador use to look down their noses at the coarse-mannered ferals, but Gangrel are no more or less inclined to devour someone else's soul than any other vampire. <br /> <br /> The only clans I see being inherently more inclined towards diablerie* are the Lasombra and Banu Haqim, whose cultures actively encourage the practice. And in the Lasombra's case it's arguably less &quot;encourage&quot; than &quot;if we legalize it, we can regulate it.&quot; <br /> <br /> * Membership in the Sabbat notwithstanding. Diablerie is probably more common among the Tzimisce, but only by dint of so much of the clan belonging to a pro-diablerie sect rather than their internal culture. The Oradea League has every cause to hate and fear diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:48:21-07:00","id":1446832,"title":"","content":"Ravnos see destroying (diablerizing) high humanity vampires as a duty. <br /> <br /> I would say Tzmisce and Tremere are quite high up the list. <br /> toreador are probably quite low, relative to their numbers. They're too social and it's weird for a lot of them to enter a retreat. Plus their clan culture is... competitive than co-operative, and often rather petty. Jealousy may drive many to diablerize, but you arent attending any parties after that. Ventrue in contrast probably just want to hide the diablerist away for PR reasons because they're all in it together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T14:10:52-07:00","id":1446848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1446832#post1446832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos see destroying (diablerizing) high humanity vampires as a duty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue less Ravnos and more the Path of Paradox followers because Path users are inherently assholes. Mind you, I couldn't tell the difference between the &quot;corrupted&quot; Paradox psychopath and the &quot;legitimate&quot; Paradox psychopaths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say Tzmisce and Tremere are quite high up the list. </div> </div> </div>Do we mean real Tzimisce or Sabbat traitors? I doubt Tremere commit diablerie much after the initial round. They're always playing the Camarilla toadies now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:36:59-07:00","id":1446861,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about culture so much as availability and ease of getting away with it. Gangrel are the most likely to run into each other alone, miles from any witnesses. And once the deed is done, they have the greatest ease avoiding auspex types long enough for the lines to fade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T20:48:04-07:00","id":1446900,"title":"","content":"From what I recall Gangrel have a sort of informal culture of gathers where most in a region are known to each other and nonlethal fights establish pecking order when such is necessary. I don't think that lends itself to the hatred and scheming that tends to go along with a lot of diablerie instances. And if one takes the animalistic predator angle, well, name me prey that's more risky than another Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:12:28-07:00","id":1446942,"title":"","content":"As a percentage thing, the most diablerie-happy 'clan' would seem to be the Salubri (Healers), since they maintain their membership of exactly seven by always diablerising their sites.<br /> <br /> If course, if you're speaking pure numbers, one of the larger clans might win that just because of the law of averages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:04:49-07:00","id":1446969,"title":"","content":"The 7 thing is legend, not truth. The Majority of healer Salubri, like the Baali, just pretend to be other clans. Also I'd say the 7 really only diab once per member...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:12:23-07:00","id":1446970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1446969#post1446969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 7 thing is legend, not truth. The Majority of healer Salubri, like the Baali, just pretend to be other clans. Also I'd say the 7 really only diab once per member...</div> </div> </div> </div>Once per member is plenty if everyone does it (hence 100%). If we're looking at frequency rather than percentage, the numbers are a bit different.<br /> <br /> As to the seven... It depends on which edition, I guess? The 7 were the main Salubri 'clan' in Revised, and everyone else was antitribu, Wu Zao, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-04-2021, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:38:19-07:00","id":1446974,"title":"","content":"It might not be practical or desirable for Gangrel to be <i>habitual </i>diablerists, but it's easier to jump a lone traveller and get away with it than a kindred with a sire, a coterie, acquaintances and a prince.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu could diablerise each other without other kindred finding out, but there's a good chance every other <i>Nosferatu</i> will find out, which could be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T12:35:54-07:00","id":1447022,"title":"","content":"I would argue less becuase they don\u00b4t care that much about power and more about survival.<br /> <br /> The more likely to be diablerist are sabbat bloodlines becuase they live in the city where court games happen and vampires are concentrated , their disciplines are make for hunting instead of surviving (Protean , Celerity , Obfuscate) and their sect encourages diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:12:37-07:00","id":1447042,"title":"","content":"I think an issue that comes into play is how easy is it supposed to be to know how to diablerize someone in your chronicles?<br /> <br /> We, as the readers of sourcebooks written to play a game, have a wealth of knowledge about diablerie from a game mechanics perspective, but I have doubts as to how well known both the practice and the practical details of doing it are known IC, at least outside the Sabbat and Assamites. Like many things, we have a different perspective in early Vampire than we do in later editions when it became much more common.<br /> <br /> One aspect of diablerie is that you continue to diablerize the vampire after that vampire's vitae has run out. You just don't drain the vampire of her blood points, but proceed to health levels as the vampire drains the &quot;life force&quot; and then finally consumes the &quot;soul&quot; of the vampire.<br /> <br /> So I think it's important to realize there are two related, but distinct terms of diablerie. One is just &quot;a vampire who has drunk all the vitae of another vampire&quot; and the second is &quot;a vampire who has performed the actual complete act of draining another vampire's vitae, life force and consumed the Fire Within.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am sure there are many vampires who know the first definition, but not the details of the second. Even if they are determined cannibals to drain the vitae of other vampires, they won't ever truly succeed in diablerie. They'll just put the other vampire into torpor.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, even those who learn the real steps that need to be done may stop well short of actual diablerie. You need to make Strength checks at Difficulty 9. As readers who have read out of character what needs to be done, we can have our characters act accordingly. How many 9s have I rolled? Is it enough to eliminate all their Health Levels? If not, I will continue to such even though I am now on my tenth extended roll on Strength and may need to do a dozen more to get all the nines I need. But that is applying out of character knowledge to a scene. What would happen if the ST rolled all those dice for you? When would you stop? What if you didn't know the goal was to eliminate Health Levels, and was just told to &quot;keep going&quot; after all the vitae was drained? In practice, a lot of vampires, especially those doing it for the first time, will give up long before they complete diablerie and get any benefits. Or perhaps they did succeed, but on a vampire of inferior generation and therefore gained no power from it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if there is a large number of vampires (at least outside the Sabbat and Assamites) who believe diablerie giving you power is a myth like Golconda. They've &quot;done&quot; it (improperly) and know they've gotten nothing out of it. It tastes delicious, but it doesn't do squat for you. Those rumors have to be out there just as much as the good rumors. I imagine most of the successful Blood Hunts of the Camarilla end long before the victim is truly diablerized.<br /> <br /> I remember one detail in the original Chicago By Night quite well. And that was how Alan Sovereign had heard a rumor that killing one's sire and drinking his blood makes a vampire more powerful. There's a lot of implied assumptions in that statement. Sovereign is a fairly influential and knowledgeable vampire albeit a neonate. He's one of the prince's brood and the main lieutenant of Horatio Ballard. He has a Secrets score of B- (he pretty much knows everything concerning vampires in Chicago except the politics within the Primogen and the struggle between Helena and Menele. Like a lot of character traits in CbN, not everything makes sense and there are lots of vampires that know more than Sovereign, but he's clearly in the middle of the listed NPCs.) <br /> <br /> He's an example of a clearly well informed vampire. Despite that he has 1) never previously been exposed to the concept of diablerie before, 2) only recently heard about it as a rumor, and 3) the rumor is wrong (and vague) on details. I think a lot of vampires, especially non-elders, should be like that. And the elders who do know, why the hell would they ever explain that to anyone?<br /> <br /> So I think there is a big difference between the first definition, which many vampires will know as drinking the blood of a vampire, and the actual secret definition (that it gives you real benefits and has a special procedure you must follow to do so).<br /> <br /> Given the social stigma of such cannibalism and the effects it has on one's aura (though that may only happen after true diablerie, but I think it would be interesting to have such auras be seen after failed attempts at it), there may be much less diablerie done outside the Sabbat then one may thinks. <br /> <br /> Characters in the setting don't have an official rulebook and setting guide like we do. As such, I think STs can have a wide range of options of how well known the details of the diablerie concept are in the general vampire population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:16:50-07:00","id":1447224,"title":"","content":"The main problem that I have is that the above depiction does not seem to jive with the notion of &quot;impulse/frenzy diablerie&quot; that I have picked up on over the years. If you accept the idea that a Vampire under the influence of the Beast can figure out how to diablerize another Vampire, it seems odd to have it require some special process that lucid Vampires have trouble figuring out. Diablerie might be difficult in terms of effort required, but the sense I've always gotten is that the act itself is straightforward: after it seems like every last drop of Vitae is gone, just keep on drinking, like someone trying to squeeze the last drops out of a waterskin in the desert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:10:55-07:00","id":1447251,"title":"","content":"Well, it'd be almost inconceivable to walk around with a gun in London as a civilian. A lot of people don't even know you can legally own a gun in the UK, with a few people even believing that all UK police do not carry firearms (most of them don't, but there certainly are a few where necessary). <br /> Meanwhile in Texas... <br /> <br /> If you live in a well ordered city (which are the majority of Cities, but the minority of cities players operate in) Nobody's going to know about Diablerie except a few elders. If you live in some Anarch hellhole, Diablerie is going to be more obvious than who's in charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T16:09:12-07:00","id":1447291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1447224#post1447224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem that I have is that the above depiction does not seem to jive with the notion of &quot;impulse/frenzy diablerie&quot; that I have picked up on over the years. If you accept the idea that a Vampire under the influence of the Beast can figure out how to diablerize another Vampire, it seems odd to have it require some special process that lucid Vampires have trouble figuring out. Diablerie might be difficult in terms of effort required, but the sense I've always gotten is that the act itself is straightforward: after it seems like every last drop of Vitae is gone, just keep on drinking, like someone trying to squeeze the last drops out of a waterskin in the desert.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this can still be compatible. The Beast doesn't &quot;know&quot; anything. It is just reacting on predatory instinct. I would say that as long as the frenzied diablerist keeps rolling 9 on their Strength check to consume the life force, the Beast keeps pushing the vampire on. The moment it fails its Strength check, it doesn't get any reward and would stop, and then it would move on the next thing. Because once the rush isn't fed, why keep going? We don't expect vampires to keep feeding on humans after their blood is gone, so without reward the vampire should move on. Since rolling against difficulty 9 is hard, it fails most of the time. But there would be cases where a 9 is rolled every round until all the Health Levels would go. So even in my system, it would still be possible for true diablerie under frenzy.<br /> <br /> This is really a matter of taste. To a lot of players, diablerie should be omnipresent in the setting. I prefer things to be more mysterious that PCs can learn during the game, and to provide a starker contrast between the Sabbat and the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T17:22:53-07:00","id":1447304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1447291#post1447291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this can still be compatible. The Beast doesn't &quot;know&quot; anything. It is just reacting on predatory instinct. I would say that as long as the frenzied diablerist keeps rolling 9 on their Strength check to consume the life force, the Beast keeps pushing the vampire on. The moment it fails its Strength check, it doesn't get any reward and would stop, and then it would move on the next thing. Because once the rush isn't fed, why keep going? We don't expect vampires to keep feeding on humans after their blood is gone, so without reward the vampire should move on. Since rolling against difficulty 9 is hard, it fails most of the time. But there would be cases where a 9 is rolled every round until all the Health Levels would go. So even in my system, it would still be possible for true diablerie under frenzy.<br /> <br /> This is really a matter of taste. To a lot of players, diablerie should be omnipresent in the setting. I prefer things to be more mysterious that PCs can learn during the game, and to provide a starker contrast between the Sabbat and the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definitely agree that it is really a matter of taste <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I wasn't really thinking about the mechanics of diablerie when I posted, so I hadn't considered things like difficulties and rolls, but I can see how it could be easy for many people to fail the roll and not know there is a reason to keep trying, so fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T02:14:37-07:00","id":1447373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans#post1446763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they are out on the road much more than other clans, isolated, no witnesses if two Gangrel run across each other and one decides to eat the other. I'd think diablerie would be pretty common.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Gangrel are often mistaken for one of the more lawless and anarchic clans, like the modern Brujah. In fact they have as rich a culture as the Ventrue, and in their own way are extremely rigorous and picky with whom they embrace. Althings/Gatherings are the way in which Gangrel Elders transmit their wisdom and culture down to the younger Kindred, and they police their own ranks for proper behavior as much as any other Clan. The type of Gangrel who would consider Diablerie probably falls out of this culture and becomes <i>antitribu</i> (&quot;Country&quot; Gangrel), and this happens no more than the rate at which other disaffected kindred join the Sabbat's ranks. True the Gangrel are often alone and unsupervised for long periods, but this only comes after they pass through their fledgelinghood and prove they not only have the hardihood to survive, but the wisdom to respect their Elders and the Clan's culture. I don't see any reason to suggest they have a higher rate of misbehavior than the Nosferatu warrens or Ventrue peerage, which enforce their own codes and mores by shunning or expelling those who flaunt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T02:57:21-07:00","id":1447378,"title":"","content":"Gangrel may have a rich culture, but it's a counter-culture; they might as well be one of the more lawless and anarchic clans, though in this they're banded together against the world rather than against eachother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:42:01-07:00","id":1447396,"title":"","content":"I'd argue Gangrel would be <i>less</i> likely to do it than other clans put in the same circumstance. Gangrel, for what they are, are insular, largely isolated, tightly-knit, communal, aren't necessarily out for power for its own sake, and their clan culture is built on a latticework of social connections and oral tradition. It's not the case they're unique among vampire clans in holding any of those traits, but the <i>combination</i> of those traits is what matters. They may be individualistic survivalists, but the clan-wide social network provides survival opportunities unavailable to a &quot;true&quot; loner and a smart Gangrel isn't going to decline those opportunities to choose an increase of personal power of potentially less utility.<br /> <br /> This isn't about whether a would-be diablerist is going to get caught in or after the act. It's about the value the potential diablerie victim brings to the clan, and by extension the individual, and the potential ramifications and harm done by removing the victim from the aforementioned social latticework. The victim may have news or tales to tell of value to others in the clan that would be lost to diablerie. The victim may have knowledge of disciplines they may be able to teach others in the clan, which may well be lost to diablerie. The victim may be another vampire's messenger, and if removed from the social latticework a valuable lifeline of information spread in the clan may be lost.<br /> <br /> Yeah, if two Gangrel meet in the wild, they're going to figure out where in the pecking order each sits, however they choose to do it. But diablerie? too high risk, too little reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:28:20-07:00","id":1447432,"title":"","content":"Although it probably is because I see the Gangrel as the mostly (or stereotypically) anti-society vampires, but whose own clan laws, customs and gatherings is the most respected by its members (baring perhaps Tzimisce lords), I think they would mostly not eat each other out like that. They might fight a lot, but hardly would diablerize one another, mostly because I don't believe diablerie is a mindless thing, at least not most of the time, and well I think they are happy with only &quot;one&quot; Beast inside them, and wouldn't want another. Of course, there would be those that say that to not diablerize a vampire you defeated is a waste of prey, or that is a right of the winner to take it. <br /> So it would not only be something deliberate, but something either part of the convictions of one Gangrel, an antitribu way of going full bloodhound (antitribu not necessarily meaning Sabbat, only going against the creeds and traditions of your clan), or an accord between two dueling Gangrel. Maybe something like a Court of Blood (only a lot less authoritarian and regular of course) can be had in a Thing or Althing when one Gangrel is clearly causing much trouble for all, or even is causing shame for the Clan (if the local Gangrel believe in such a thing). There might be some more shaman or spiritual-like Ferals that believe it is entirely wrong to eat the spirit of other beings, or at least the spirit of those with tainted souls; or maybe they go full dark shaman and eat the spirit of the wicked to become full of power and without regret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:06:23-07:00","id":1447456,"title":"","content":"That seems like a racist myth made to hate and Gangral. Going by clan weakness along the Brujah should have the highest frequency of Soul eating considering their clan flaw of Anger. But the Sabbat clans probably have the most dialbleroest because the Sabbat doesn\u2019t ban Dialbre","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:24:45-07:00","id":1447463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1447456#post1447456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a racist myth made to hate and Gangral. Going by clan weakness along the Brujah should have the highest frequency of Soul eating considering their clan flaw of Anger. But the Sabbat clans probably have the most dialbleroest because the Sabbat doesn\u2019t ban Dialbre</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't about race, it's about vampires being vampires under circumstances where there is no interference, and no witnesses, and therefore no consequences to doing something evil for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T08:44:02-07:00","id":1447580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1447463#post1447463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't about race, it's about vampires being vampires under circumstances where there is no interference, and no witnesses, and therefore no consequences to doing something evil for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's do the math on this.<br /> <br /> One Gangrel meets another on the road. Those Gangrel may or may not know each other, and if they don't they have no way of telling how old the other is or what generation. An attempt to diablerize means the claws and fangs come out, and blood gets spent to buff and fuel disciplines. More likely than not, if the vampire was worth diablerizing to begin with, the victor is limping away low on blood and nursing a nasty aggravated wound or two.<br /> <br /> That means the victor has to hunt, spend a night or two healing up, and hunt even more to compensate for the blood they spent healing aggravated wounds, and spend even more blood to fuel earth melds and animal forms in the meantime. And all that equates to vulnerability, on the road, more likely than not in lupine territory where the most fearsome pack hunters in the whole-ass World of Darkness are going to waste no time picking up a blood and scent trail from the scene of a lethal fight or starving-Gangrel-wild-animal-massacre to...wherever the diablerist Gangrel <i>thinks</i> is safe. And flight form is absolutely no insurance against that.<br /> <br /> A measly drop in generation is cold comfort to a Gangrel who gets dug out of the soil at noon by a pack of werewolves a day or two later, because they were too injured and too hungry to get a safe distance away from the scene of the crime.<br /> <br /> And for what? A dead Gangrel is a dead Gangrel. That's one fewer messenger, one fewer story-teller and carrier of the clan's oral traditions, one fewer clan mate to potentially call on in times of hardship, and one fewer clan-mate to find fledglings and train in turn. Being counter-cultural and individualist doesn't mean Gangrel lack a civic mindset, or can't see the big picture.<br /> <br /> In fact, being counter-cultural and individualist means Gangrel have to have an <i>incredibly</i> well-honed sense of risk-to-reward merely to survive, and there's <i>no</i> scenario in which one Gangrel meets another on the road where the reward of diablerie meets or exceeds the risks of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:20:43-07:00","id":1447628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1447463#post1447463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't about race, it's about vampires being vampires under circumstances where there is no interference, and no witnesses, and therefore no consequences to doing something evil for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I was using \u201cracist\u201d to mean judging others on in born traits of a different person, I guess Clannist. And it sounds similar to the Statistics that racist throw about how black people commit 50% more crime then whites on average","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T16:02:15-07:00","id":1447652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446763-do-gangrel-diablerize-each-other-more-than-other-clans?p=1447628#post1447628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I was using \u201cracist\u201d to mean judging others on in born traits of a different person, I guess Clannist. And it sounds similar to the Statistics that racist throw about how black people commit 50% more crime then whites on average</div> </div> </div> </div>......wuuuuhhh? I'm talking about how Gangrel are much more likely to encounter each other alone and miles from other vampires witnessing/interfering/judging what they do. I never suggested that Gangrel are inherently more evil than other vampires. I'm saying they are equally evil and far more likely to be in circumstances where they can indulge that particular evil without consequence. This is about the lack of law-enforcement they have to deal with, not about Gangrel being born more moustache-twirly.<br /> <br /> That said, this is a game in which the different clans ACTUALLY suffer clan compulsions and have actual inherited personality traits like a tendency towards rage or madness, so IF I was claiming that Gangrel were more evil, comparing that to racism would still be absurd. But since I'm not making such a claim, it is a doubly absurd comparison.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T05:33:14-07:00","id":1447796,"title":"","content":"Ignoring nonsense like clan compulsions, the clans are still a very self selective bunch, and their strengths and weaknesses further accentuate what kind of vampires they are going to be, and this is all before clans build their own cultures which further typify the bloodline. Vampire 'Clannism' is in many ways more natural and potent than ideas of racism. Race is an accident of birth, clan is a matter of who you are both before and after the embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T04:41:40-07:00","id":1448114,"title":"","content":"I just had a thought (if you can excuse the V5 diatribe) <br /> <br /> In V5, the Gangrel are going to be the absolute least likely clan to diablerize. Obviously, there's the angle of -Animal Blood is an important fallback for my diet and I need the resonance so gaining blood potency is an absolutely terrible idea for me-. But there's also the shift of Diablerie from -I need to do this to push the glass ceiling and raise my limits- towards -This'll give me a quick and dirty pile of XP to spend on my disciplines- <br /> The issue with that, for the Gangrel, is that they're generally the clan with the LEAST amount of pressure on them. Political pressure? Pack up and leave. Hunters? Well they can narrow your sleeping ground to within... four killometres, good luck with the digging. Your domain and herd is threatened? They're a convenience, you don't need them. Gangrel are survivors, they're self reliant, they always have something to fall back to. The Ventrue and Tzmisce are rather extreme counterexamples, but 'normal' clans like Toreador, Brujah or Malkavians draw a lot of their worth from what's around them, often feeling it's better to die on the hill than to start over. Another vampire feels threatened, they believe they have to defend, they have to accumulate, and diablerie is a radical idea that'll grant them the boost they'll need over their enemies. A Gangrel will very much fight, if she thinks she can win, but she's more happy to cut her losses and run before she needs to consider risky ideas like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}